-The next step is adding {{ ohpc }} components to the *compute* nodes that at this
-point are running basic OSes. This process will leverage two {{ confluent }}-provided
-commands: `nodeshell` to run `{{ pkgmgr }}` installer on all the
-nodes in parallel and `nodersync` to distribute configuration files from the
-SMS to the *compute* nodes.
-
-To do this, repositories on the *compute* nodes need to be configured
-properly.
-
-{{ confluent }} has automatically setup an OS repository on the SMS and configured the
-nodes to use it, but it has also enabled online OS repositories.
-
-
-Next, we also add the OHPC repository to the compute nodes
-
-<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
-<!-- ohpc_comment_header Setup nodes repositories and Install OHPC components \ref{sec:add_components} -->
-```bash
-# Add OpenHPC repo
-[sms]# {{ chrootinstall }} \
-	http://repos.openhpc.community/OpenHPC/4/{{ ostree }}/x86_64/\
-ohpc-release-4-1.{{ ostag }}.x86_64.rpm
-```
-<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
-
-The *compute* nodes also need access to the EPEL repository, a required
-dependency for {{ ohpc }} packages.
-
-<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
-<!-- ohpc_comment_header Configure access to EPEL repo -->
-```bash
-# Add epel repo
-[sms]# {{ chrootinstall }} epel-release
-
-```
-<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
-
-
-Additionally, a workaround is needed for {{ ohpc }} documentation files,
-which are installed into a read-only NFS share /opt/ohpc/pub. Any package
-attempting to write to that directory will fail to install. The following
-prevents that by directing `rpm` not to install documentation files on
-the *compute* nodes:
-
-<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
-```bash
-[sms]# nodeshell compute echo -e %_excludedocs 1 \>\> ~/.rpmmacros
-```
-<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
-
-Now {{ ohpc }} and other cluster-related software components can be
-installed on the nodes. The first step is to install a base compute package
-and disable the firewall on the compute nodes:
-<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
-<!-- ohpc_comment_header Add OpenHPC base components to compute image -->
-```bash
-# Install compute node base meta-package
-[sms]# {{ chrootinstall }} ohpc-base-compute git
-# Disable firewall for computes
-[sms]# nodeshell compute systemctl disable --now firewalld
-```
-<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
-
-Next, we can include additional components:
