-With the resource manager enabled for production usage, users should now be
-able to run jobs. To demonstrate this, we will add a `test` user on the *master*
-host that can be used to run an example job.
-
-<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
-```bash
-[sms]# useradd -m test
-```
-<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
-
-Next, the user's credentials need to be distributed across the cluster.
-{{ confluent }}'s `nodeapply` has a merge functionality that adds new entries into
-credential files on *compute* nodes:
-
-<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
-```bash
-# Create a sync file for pushing user credentials to the nodes
-[sms]# echo "/etc/passwd -> /etc/passwd" >> \
-	/var/lib/confluent/public/os/{{ confluentprofile }}/syncfiles
-[sms]# echo "/etc/group -> /etc/group" >> \
-	/var/lib/confluent/public/os/{{ confluentprofile }}/syncfiles
-
-# Use Confluent to distribute credentials to nodes
-[sms]# nodeapply -F compute
-```
-<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
