diff --git a/docs/recipes/install/poc-markdown/common/slurm_startup.md.j2 b/docs/recipes/install/poc-markdown/common/slurm_startup.md.j2
deleted file mode 100644
index 7aa50e1a7..000000000
--- a/docs/recipes/install/poc-markdown/common/slurm_startup.md.j2
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,30 +0,0 @@
-In an earlier section, the Slurm resource manager was installed
-and configured for use on both the **master** host and **compute** node
-instances. With the cluster nodes up and functional, we can now startup the
-resource manager services in preparation for running user jobs. Generally, this
-is a two-step process that requires starting up the controller daemons on the **master** host and the client daemons on each of the **compute** hosts.
-Note that Slurm leverages the use of the **munge** library to provide
-authentication services and this daemon also needs to be running on all hosts
-within the resource management pool.
-The following commands can be used to startup the necessary services to support
-resource management under Slurm.
-
-<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
-<!-- ohpc_comment_header Allow for optional sleep to wait for provisioning to complete -->
-<!-- ohpc_command sleep "${provision_wait}" -->
-<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
-
-<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
-<!-- ohpc_comment_header Resource Manager Startup -->
-```bash
-# Start munge and slurm controller on master host
-[sms]# systemctl enable munge
-[sms]# systemctl enable slurmctld
-[sms]# systemctl start munge
-[sms]# systemctl start slurmctld
-
-# Start slurm clients on compute hosts
-[sms]# pdsh -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" systemctl start munge
-[sms]# pdsh -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" systemctl start slurmd
-```
-<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/docs/recipes/install/poc-markdown/common/slurm_startup_confluent.md.j2 b/docs/recipes/install/poc-markdown/common/slurm_startup_confluent.md.j2
deleted file mode 100644
index 8af1f6ea4..000000000
--- a/docs/recipes/install/poc-markdown/common/slurm_startup_confluent.md.j2
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,54 +0,0 @@
-In the previous section, the {{ SLURM }} resource manager was
-installed and configured on the *master* host. {{ SLURM }} clients were also
-installed, but have not been configured yet. To do so, {{ SLURM }} and
-`munge` configuration files need to be copied to the nodes. This can be
-accomplished as follows:
-
-<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
-<!-- ohpc_comment_header Resource Manager Startup \ref{sec:rms_startup} -->
-```bash
-[sms]# nodersync /etc/slurm/slurm.conf compute:/etc/slurm/slurm.conf
-[sms]# nodersync /etc/munge/munge.key compute:/etc/munge/munge.key
-```
-<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
-
-
-With {{ SLURM }} configured, we can now startup the
-resource manager services in preparation for running user jobs. Generally, this
-is a two-step process that requires starting up the controller daemons on the *master* host and the client daemons on each of the *compute* hosts.
-Note that {{ SLURM }} leverages the use of the *munge* library to provide
-authentication services and this daemon also needs to be running on all hosts
-within the resource management pool.
-The following commands can be used to startup the necessary services to support
-resource management under {{ SLURM }}.
-
-<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
-```bash
-# Start munge and slurm controller on master host
-[sms]# systemctl enable munge
-[sms]# systemctl enable slurmctld
-[sms]# systemctl start munge
-[sms]# systemctl start slurmctld
-
-# Start slurm clients on compute hosts
-[sms]# nodeshell compute systemctl enable munge
-[sms]# nodeshell compute systemctl enable slurmd
-[sms]# nodeshell compute systemctl start munge
-[sms]# nodeshell compute systemctl start slurmd
-```
-<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
-
-After this, check status of the nodes within {{ SLURM }} by using the
-`sinfo` command. All compute nodes should be in an *idle* state
-(without asterisk). If the state is reported as *unknown*, the following
-might help:
-
-```bash
-[sms]# scontrol update partition=normal state=idle
-```
-
-In case of additional {{ SLURM }} issues, ensure that the configuration file fits
-your hardware and that it is identical across the nodes. Also, verify
-that {{ SLURM }} user id is the same on the SMS and *compute* nodes. You may
-also consult
-[{{ SLURM }} Troubleshooting Guide](https://slurm.schedmd.com/troubleshoot.html).
diff --git a/docs/recipes/install/poc-markdown/common/syslog.md.j2 b/docs/recipes/install/poc-markdown/common/syslog.md.j2
deleted file mode 100644
index 1145aaa4d..000000000
--- a/docs/recipes/install/poc-markdown/common/syslog.md.j2
